From: IrfanMohammad <irfan@graphiant.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Jul 2023 18:17:37 +0000
Subject: Add change_sub with minimal locks

- do not lock mods longer than necessary for adding enabled change_sub

    Addition of change_sub happens in 5 important steps w.r.t locks
    1. change_sub write lock- This will prevent any new events from
       being published for this module
    2. modules lock, invoke enabled callback() and unlock
    3. add sub to ext_shm and downgrade change_sub to read lock- Any
       writers can now notify subscribers, but this subscription is not
       ready yet.
    4. acquire subs_lock write mode, add subscr to subscription
       structure to make it visible to handler thread
    5. release write subs_lock, then change_sub read lock

    Previously, we held module locks beyond Step 2.
    This was to prevent losing events after Step 2 and before Step 5.

    Since the fix for ENG-3166 and ENG-3839, We always check for any
    missed events during Step 4, and notify the handler thread.

    Because of this, holding onto modules lock is no longer necessary.

cherry-picked from 0067-Locking-improvements-for-subscriptions.patch
